{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "SfclayRevParameters",
  "description": "Scheme constants of WRF's revised MM5 surface-layer scheme (sf_sfclay_physics = 1, `sf_sfclayrev_run` in phys/physics_mmm/sf_sfclayrev.F90, WRF 4.8 / NCAR MMM-physics; Jimenez et al. 2012), transcribed from the module `parameter` declarations and the in-line literals of the kernel so that no tuning constant is written inline in the physics. Mounted by the SfclayRev component as subsystem `par`. Values are the nominal (decimal) values written in the Fortran source. The coefficients of the similarity functions themselves (Cheng-Brutsaert 6.1/2.5 and 5.3/1.1, Kansas 16, free-convection 10/34 and the 0.33 exponent) and the psi lookup-table discretisation (step 0.01, 1000 nodes) are properties of the published functions, not tuning constants, and live with the functions in similarity_functions.esm. NOTE (FORTRAN_BUGS.md N2/N10): the kernel's literals are default-real, so a real64 build runs with their single-precision roundings (e.g. 1/2.5 = 0.4000000059604645, sqrt(3.) and atan(1.) evaluated in real32, the lookup-table nodes float(n)*0.01 rounded to real32); the SfclayRev tests document the resulting O(1e-7) relative mismatch in their tolerances rather than reproducing the rounding here.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wrf",
   "surface-layer",
   "sfclayrev",
   "scheme-constants"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Jimenez, P. A., Dudhia, J., Gonzalez-Rouco, J. F., Navarro, J., Montavez, J. P., and Garcia-Bustamante, E. (2012). A revised scheme for the WRF surface layer formulation. Mon. Wea. Rev. 140, 898-918."
   },
   {
    "citation": "Cheng, Y. and Brutsaert, W. (2005). Flux-profile relationships for wind speed and temperature in the stable atmospheric boundary layer. Bound.-Layer Meteor. 114, 519-538."
   },
   {
    "citation": "Fairall, C. W., Bradley, E. F., Hare, J. E., Grachev, A. A., and Edson, J. B. (2003). Bulk parameterization of air-sea fluxes: updates and verification for the COARE algorithm. J. Climate 16, 571-591."
   },
   {
    "citation": "Jimenez, P. A. and Dudhia, J. (2018). On the need to modify the sea surface roughness formulation over shallow waters. J. Appl. Meteor. Climatol. 57, 1101-1110."
   },
   {
    "citation": "WRF 4.8 phys/physics_mmm/sf_sfclayrev.F90 lines 12-16 (module parameters), 181-183 (xka, prt, salinity_factor), 300, 333, 348, 357, 360-362, 391, 399, 499-505, 539-543, 603, 643, 675, 737-739, 831-833, 848-854, 957-967, 1129-1139 (in-line literals)."
   }
  ]
 },
 "models": {
  "SfclayRevParameters": {
   "variables": {
    "vconvc": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "Coefficient of the Beljaars (1994) convective velocity scale over land (module parameter vconvc)."
    },
    "czo": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0185,
     "description": "Charnock coefficient of the sea-surface roughness (module parameter czo)."
    },
    "ozo": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 1.59e-05,
     "description": "Smooth-flow sea-surface roughness offset used by the isftcflx AHW roughness (module parameter ozo)."
    },
    "varf_min": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 5.0,
     "description": "Minimum subgrid orography standard deviation for the KIM turbulent orographic form drag (module parameter varf_min; the branch is not transcribed, see FORTRAN_BUGS.md B3)."
    },
    "ca_square": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.16,
     "description": "Squared drag constant 0.4^2 of the KIM form drag (module parameter ca_square)."
    },
    "xka": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^2/s",
     "default": 2.4e-05,
     "description": "Molecular diffusivity of water vapour in the land psiq roughness sublayer term karman ust z/xka (local parameter xka)."
    },
    "prt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "Turbulent Prandtl number in the temperature scale mol = karman dtg/(psit prt) (local parameter prt)."
    },
    "salinity_factor": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.98,
     "description": "Saturation vapour pressure reduction over salt water (local parameter salinity_factor)."
    },
    "z_landsub": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.01,
     "description": "Effective roughness of the land moisture sublayer (literal 0.01 in zl over land, lines 333, 527, 859)."
    },
    "dx_ref": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 5000.0,
     "description": "Grid-length scale of the Mahrt and Sun (1995) subgrid velocity vsgd = 0.32 max(dx/5000 - 1, 0)^0.33 (line 360)."
    },
    "vsgd_coef": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.32,
     "description": "Prefactor of the Mahrt and Sun subgrid velocity (line 360)."
    },
    "vsgd_exp": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.33,
     "description": "Exponent of the Mahrt and Sun subgrid velocity and of the Beljaars convective velocity (lines 348, 360)."
    },
    "wspd_min": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.1,
     "description": "Floor of the effective wind speed (line 362)."
    },
    "br_max": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 250.0,
     "description": "Clamp of |Ri_b| passed to the z/L solver (lines 391, 402)."
    },
    "ust_min_land": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.001,
     "description": "Floor of u* over land, and the threshold below which the first-guess z/L = Ri_b ln((z+z0)/z0) is used instead of the solver (lines 399, 797)."
    },
    "psi_limit_frac": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.9,
     "description": "Unstable-regime cap psi <= 0.9 ln((z+z0)/z0) that keeps the flux denominators away from zero (lines 499-505)."
    },
    "dtthx_min": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "default": 1e-05,
     "description": "Minimum |thx - thgb| below which the heat exchange coefficient flhc is set to zero (line 865)."
    },
    "cpm_qfac": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.8,
     "description": "Moist heat capacity factor cpm = cp (1 + 0.8 qv) (line 300)."
    },
    "visc_a": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^2/s",
     "default": 1.32e-05,
     "description": "Kinematic viscosity of air at 0 degC in visc = (1.32 + 0.009 (T - 273.15)) 1e-5 (lines 539, 640, 731)."
    },
    "visc_b": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^2/(s*K)",
     "default": 9e-08,
     "description": "Temperature slope of the kinematic viscosity of air (0.009 1e-5 per K)."
    },
    "visc_t0": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "default": 273.15,
     "description": "Reference temperature of the viscosity fit."
    },
    "z0t_fairall_coef": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 5.5e-05,
     "description": "Fairall et al. (2003) thermal roughness over water z0t = 5.5e-5 Re*^-0.6 (line 541)."
    },
    "z0t_fairall_exp": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": -0.6,
     "description": "Roughness-Reynolds exponent of the Fairall thermal roughness."
    },
    "z0t_water_max": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0001,
     "description": "Upper bound of the Fairall thermal roughness (line 542)."
    },
    "z0t_water_min": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 2e-09,
     "description": "Lower bound of the Fairall thermal roughness (line 543)."
    },
    "z0q_isftcflx1": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0001,
     "description": "Fixed moisture roughness over water for isftcflx = 1 (line 603)."
    },
    "garratt_k": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.4,
     "description": "von Karman constant as hard-wired in the Garratt (1992) roughness sublayer terms for isftcflx = 2 (lines 643, 675)."
    },
    "garratt_a": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 7.3,
     "description": "Brutsaert (1975) coefficient 7.3 in ln(z0/z0t) = k (7.3 Re*^(1/4) Pr^(1/2) - 5)."
    },
    "garratt_b": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 5.0,
     "description": "Brutsaert (1975) offset 5."
    },
    "prandtl_garratt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.71,
     "description": "Prandtl number of the Garratt thermal roughness."
    },
    "schmidt_garratt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.6,
     "description": "Schmidt number of the Garratt moisture roughness."
    },
    "czil_ref": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.1,
     "description": "Traditional Zilitinkevich coefficient for iz0tlnd = 2 (line 739)."
    },
    "czil_cz_exp": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": -0.4,
     "description": "Chen and Zhang (2009) exponent in czil = 10^(-0.4 z0/0.07) for iz0tlnd = 1 (line 737)."
    },
    "czil_cz_z0ref": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.07,
     "description": "Chen and Zhang (2009) roughness scale 0.07 m."
    },
    "z0_smooth_coef": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.11,
     "description": "Smooth-flow coefficient 0.11 of the sea roughness z0 = czo u*^2/g + 0.11 nu/u* (line 831)."
    },
    "nu_sea": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^2/s",
     "default": 1.5e-05,
     "description": "Kinematic viscosity used in the smooth-flow sea roughness term (line 831)."
    },
    "z0_water_max": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.00285,
     "description": "Upper bound of the sea-surface roughness (lines 833, 853)."
    },
    "z0_water_min_ahw": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 1.27e-07,
     "description": "Lower bound of the AHW (isftcflx /= 0) sea roughness (line 854)."
    },
    "ahw_ust_ref": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 1.06,
     "description": "u* scale of the AHW blending weight zw = min((u*/1.06)^0.3, 1) (line 848)."
    },
    "ahw_zw_exp": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.3,
     "description": "Exponent of the AHW blending weight."
    },
    "ahw_charnock": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.011,
     "description": "Charnock coefficient of the AHW low-wind roughness zn1 (line 849)."
    },
    "ahw_zn2_coef": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 10.0,
     "description": "Prefactor of the AHW high-wind roughness zn2 = 10 exp(-9.5 u*^(-1/3)) (line 850)."
    },
    "ahw_zn2_exp": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 9.5,
     "description": "Coefficient 9.5 of the AHW high-wind roughness exponent."
    },
    "ahw_zn2_ust_exp": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": -0.3333,
     "description": "u* exponent -0.3333 of the AHW high-wind roughness (literal -.3333, not -1/3)."
    },
    "ahw_ust_min": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.01,
     "description": "u* floor in the AHW smooth-flow term (line 851)."
    },
    "shal_depth_min": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 10.0,
     "description": "Lower clamp of the water depth in the Jimenez-Dudhia (2018) shallow-water roughness (line 1130)."
    },
    "shal_depth_max": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 100.0,
     "description": "Upper clamp of the water depth (line 1131)."
    },
    "shal_b_coef": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.03333333333333333,
     "description": "1/30 in depth_b = (1/30) ln(1260/depth) (line 1137)."
    },
    "shal_b_scale": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 1260.0,
     "description": "Depth scale 1260 m of depth_b."
    },
    "shal_c1": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 2.7,
     "description": "z0 = exp((2.7 u* - 1.8/depth_b)/(u* + 0.17/depth_b)) coefficient 2.7 (line 1138)."
    },
    "shal_c2": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 1.8,
     "description": "Coefficient 1.8 of the shallow-water roughness."
    },
    "shal_c3": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.17,
     "description": "Coefficient 0.17 of the shallow-water roughness."
    },
    "shal_z0_max": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.1,
     "description": "Upper bound of the shallow-water roughness (line 1139)."
    },
    "secant_bracket": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 5.0,
     "description": "Initial secant bracket |z/L| = 5 of the Ri_b -> z/L solver zolri (lines 957-962)."
    },
    "secant_tol": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.01,
     "description": "Termination |x1 - x2| <= 0.01 of the zolri secant iteration (line 967)."
    },
    "z_2m": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 2.0,
     "description": "Height of the 2 m temperature and moisture diagnostics (literal 2. in gz2oz0, zol2, zl2, psiq2)."
    },
    "z_10m": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 10.0,
     "description": "Height of the 10 m wind diagnostics (literal 10. in gz10oz0, zol10, zl10, psiq10)."
    },
    "unit_velocity": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "1 m/s. The kernel raises dimensioned velocities to non-integer powers (vconv = (g/T h w)^0.33, zn2 = 10 exp(-9.5 u*^-0.3333)), which is dimensionally inconsistent; the esm divides the base by this unit velocity so the expression is dimensionally consistent and numerically identical in SI."
    },
    "unit_length": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "1 m. The Jimenez-Dudhia (2018) shallow-water roughness exp((2.7 u* - 1.8/b)/(u* + 0.17/b)) is a pure number used as metres; multiplied by this unit length in the esm."
    },
    "unit_kelvin": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "1 K. The kernel's over-water convective velocity vconv = sqrt(max(tskv - thvx, 0)) takes the square root of a temperature difference and uses it as m/s (the old MM5/Wyngaard form with its coefficient 2 m/s/K^(1/2) reduced to 1 in V3.7); the esm divides by this unit temperature and multiplies by unit_velocity so the expression is dimensionally consistent and numerically identical in SI."
    }
   },
   "equations": [],
   "tests": []
  }
 }
}